Subject: [PATCH] luci-mod-network: allow reading the iwinfo device list

CBIWifiTxPowerValue falls back to `iwinfo devices` when neither the VAP
interface name nor the wifi-device section yields a usable transmit
power list (on QSDK ath12k this is the 6 GHz band: libiwinfo has no
6 GHz band, so its phy-level and per-VAP queries only return the
"not reported" sentinel).  The rpc ACL of luci-mod-network only granted
assoclist, countrylist, freqlist and txpowerlist, so that call was
denied.  `devices` is a read-only method that lists interface names;
grant it next to the other iwinfo read methods.

diff --git a/modules/luci-mod-network/root/usr/share/rpcd/acl.d/luci-mod-network.json b/modules/luci-mod-network/root/usr/share/rpcd/acl.d/luci-mod-network.json
index 002a6d085d..f0227189fc 100644
--- a/modules/luci-mod-network/root/usr/share/rpcd/acl.d/luci-mod-network.json
+++ b/modules/luci-mod-network/root/usr/share/rpcd/acl.d/luci-mod-network.json
@@ -13,7 +13,7 @@
 			},
 			"ubus": {
 				"file": [ "exec" ],
-				"iwinfo": [ "assoclist", "countrylist", "freqlist", "txpowerlist" ],
+				"iwinfo": [ "assoclist", "countrylist", "devices", "freqlist", "txpowerlist" ],
 				"luci": [ "getSwconfigFeatures", "getSwconfigPortState" ]
 			},
 			"uci": [ "dhcp", "firewall", "network", "wireless", "system" ]
